{
 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "This man sold the Brooklyn Bridge.",
   "start": 0.1,
   "end": 1.953
  },
  {
   "text": "Not once.",
   "start": 2.033,
   "end": 2.785
  },
  {
   "text": "Again and again.",
   "start": 2.845,
   "end": 3.789
  },
  {
   "text": "He'd find newcomers fresh off the boat,",
   "start": 4.089,
   "end": 5.97
  },
  {
   "text": "flash his official-looking papers,",
   "start": 6.05,
   "end": 7.882
  },
  {
   "text": "and make an offer:",
   "start": 7.962,
   "end": 8.88
  },
  {
   "text": "buy the bridge, and charge a toll to cross it.",
   "start": 8.98,
   "end": 11.413
  },
  {
   "text": "They paid him in cash.",
   "start": 11.533,
   "end": 12.721
  },
  {
   "text": "The next morning, they set up a toll booth,",
   "start": 13.021,
   "end": 15.245
  },
  {
   "text": "until the police dragged them away.",
   "start": 15.345,
   "end": 16.967
  },
  {
   "text": "He was finally caught,",
   "start": 17.267,
   "end": 18.404
  },
  {
   "text": "and spent the rest of his life in prison.",
   "start": 18.484,
   "end": 20.347
  },
  {
   "text": "But his trick lives on:",
   "start": 20.647,
   "end": 21.851
  },
  {
   "text": "If you believe that, I've got a bridge to sell you.",
   "start": 21.971,
   "end": 24.53
  }
 ],
